[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Pangolin is a tunneled AI gateway that provides easy access to local AI clusters like Ollama or vLLM for engineering teams running things like open code or cloud code. It sits in the middle and provides keyless authentication, access control, and logging so that you can keep track of'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what your team is doing and make connectivity easy. In this video, I\'ll show you how to set up Ollama with Pangolin AI gateway and get access from any computer. Pangolin will create an outbound only VPN tunnel between a private network and the gateway so that'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can access any privately hosted AI model or cluster. I\'m going to demonstrate Ollama. I already have Ollama installed on this computer and I can run Ollama run tiny llama. This will serve an OpenAI compatible endpoint locally on this computer, but if I want'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'other users to be able to access this, I would typically have to set up a VPN or give them network access to my computer. With the Pangolin gateway, we just bring it into the gateway as any other provider. So, I\'ll show you how to create the provider. If we just go back to providers, add a new provider. In'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this case, because it\'s Ollama, it\'s not one of the presets we already have, we\'ll add a custom provider. We\'ll call it Ollama. Ollama again serves an OpenAI compatible endpoint, so we\'ll add the two OpenAI capabilities. If Ollama was accessible to the Pangolin server'

[01:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'without a tunnel connection, you could just simply insert the upstream URL, but because we need to tunnel this connection in, I\'ll have to set up a site. So, we\'ll head to the sites tab and we\'ll click add site. We\'ll call this site Ollama and it\'ll give us a very easy install command here to run'

[01:13] [scene:talk]
